      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00074",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[74]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6071,
      "endIndex": 6072,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00075",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[75]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6072,
      "endIndex": 6133,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "1. What is the absolute best fabric to wear in extreme heat?",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00076",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[76]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6133,
      "endIndex": 6367,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Without a doubt, pure linen is the undisputed champion of hot weather. Because of its loose weave and hollow fibers, it allows maximum airflow and dries faster than any other fabric. Lightweight organic cotton is a very close second!",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00077",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[77]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6367,
      "endIndex": 6368,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00078",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[78]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6368,
      "endIndex": 6409,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "2. Are jeans okay to wear in the summer?",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00079",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[79]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6409,
      "endIndex": 6650,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Heavy denim is notoriously bad for hot weather because it traps heat and offers zero breathability. If you want to wear long pants in the summer, you should instantly swap your jeans for our lightweight cotton chinos or pure linen trousers.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00080",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[80]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6650,
      "endIndex": 6651,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00081",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[81]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6651,
      "endIndex": 6700,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "3. Is it okay to wear dark colors in the summer?",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00082",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[82]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6700,
      "endIndex": 6946,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "You certainly can, especially for evening events. However, during the peak daytime sun, dark colors (like black and dark navy) absorb heat and will make you feel noticeably hotter. Try to stick to whites, pastels, and light greys during the day.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00083",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[83]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6946,
      "endIndex": 6947,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00084",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[84]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6947,
      "endIndex": 6993,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "4. Can I wear shorts to a nice summer dinner?",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00085",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[85]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6993,
      "endIndex": 7268,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Yes, but execution is everything. Skip the athletic shorts or cargo shorts. A pair of well-fitted, flat-front chino shorts paired with a crisp linen shirt and a nice pair of loafers is a highly acceptable, sophisticated outfit for a warm summer evening at a nice restaurant.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00086",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[86]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 7268,
      "endIndex": 7269,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00087",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[87]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 7269,
      "endIndex": 7322,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "5. How do I stop sweat patches showing on my shirts?",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00088",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[88]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 7322,
      "endIndex": 7665,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "First, avoid tight-fitting clothes; looser fits allow air to circulate and evaporate sweat before it pools. Second, stick strictly to natural fabrics like linen and cotton. Finally, if you naturally sweat a lot, wearing a highly breathable, lightweight pure cotton undershirt can actually help absorb moisture before it hits your outer layer.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00089",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[89]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
